  "result": "The gate passed node `LVMC_11_20_060_o2` (**OK**) on the first of the 6 allowed runs. It checked all 13 witnesses.\n\n**The rule** follows the node's record exactly, and I added no readings of my own:\n- **Who it covers:** the subject must be a vehicle under `DEF-NRS-484A-320`.\n- **When it applies:** the business-or-residence-district assumption holds, and the subject is in a driveway entrance or an alley and also on a sidewalk.\n- **What it requires:** for every pedestrian other than the subject (under `DEF-NRS-484A-165`):\n  - the subject may not move faster than the 0.1 m/s halt tolerance while, at constant speeds, it and the pedestrian would come within 3 m of each other in the next 3 s;\n  - the subject's body and the pedestrian's body may not touch.\n\n**The witnesses:** I built the five planned scenes: forbid, permit, idle, blind (subject's speed hidden) and branch_1. Then I added branch_2 to branch_9 so that each condition in the rule changes the outcome of at least one scene:\n- the subject comes out of an alley instead of a driveway;\n- the subject creeps at 5 cm/s, under the tolerance, and touches a pedestrian;\n- the pedestrian walks away, so the two never get closer;\n- the closest approach is about 4.5 m, outside the 3 m clearance;\n- the area is known not to be a business or residence district;\n- the subject is still in the driveway and hasn't reached the sidewalk;\n- the subject is a bicycle, which isn't a vehicle under that definition;\n- the other road user is a car, not a pedestrian.\n\nI found nothing wrong with the node, so there is nothing to report back to the planning step.\n\nFiles are in:\n- `library/TrafficSpec/Rules/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_20_060_o2.lean`\n- `library/TrafficSpecWitness/LVMC_11/LVMC_11_20_060_o2.lean`\n- `task_result.md` (in the working directory)",
